auto std::tie(y,x) = std::make_tuple(x.zoom(),x.zoom());

You would have:
Pair::first = ZoomScoreOne(x).zoom(), Pair::second = ZoomScoreOne(x).zoom();

If pair is only just advisors for lazy evaluation on x then you didn't have to generate a new Pair::second which is exactly what you already have in Pair::first, and thus is no worse. Besides, you can still express Pair::second lazy evaluated on res.x.zoom().
